 "notes": "Shaab el Erg, the big horseshoe reef north of Hurghada, open to the south: the reef arms round the sandy lagoon with its ergs where the dolphins live, Gota Shaab el Erg (Dolphin House) at the south-west tip with the channel the dolphins use, the patch reefs of Poseidon Garden on the south side, the outer east wall and the northern tip. The named places come from dive-centre descriptions (seawolf-safari.de, divessi.com, divers-guide.com), so positions are approximate and the lagoon ergs are not drawn individually.",
